Q: Grpc client with channel whose name is derived from the stub class A: <p>I've managed to achieve this by extending the GrpcClientFactory and registering to replace the default one. I was hoping there would be a simpler way to do it, but as Max says in <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79910291/grpc-client-with-channel-whose-name-is-derived-from-the-stub-class#answer-79910528">his answer</a>, it seems that it was a deliberate design decision to not make it easy. Anyway, here's my solution:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>public class MyGrpcClientFactory extends GrpcClientFactory {

    @Override
    public &lt;S&gt; S getClient(String target, Class&lt;S&gt; type, Class&lt;?&gt; factory) {
        if (&quot;default&quot;.equals(target)) {
            target = getChannelName(type);
        }

        return super.getClient(target, type, factory);
    }

    private static String getChannelName(Class&lt;?&gt; type) {
        String name = type.getEnclosingClass().getSimpleName();
        name = name.substring(0, name.indexOf(&quot;Grpc&quot;));
        // Change to kebab-case.
        return String.join(&quot;-&quot;, StringUtils.splitByCharacterTypeCamelCase(name)).toLowerCase();
    }

    /**
     * Registers the AssetTestGrpcClientFactory so that it replaces the standard GrpcClientFactory.
     */
    public static class Registrar implements BeanRegistrar {

        @Override
        public void register(BeanRegistry registry, Environment env) {
            registry.registerBean(
                    GrpcClientFactory.class.getName(), MyGrpcClientFactory.class, BeanRegistry.Spec::primary);
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then you have to import the Registrar into your <code>@Configuration</code> class:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@Import(MyGrpcClientFactory.Registrar.class)
</code></pre>

Q: Highcharts (Angular) - For Pie chart, hide the datalabel if it is overflowing out of its slice A: <p>Thanks for sharing.</p>
<p>This is a tricky task; you are close with your code. Here is sample prepared in VanillaJS:</p>
<pre><code>chart: {
    events: {
      render: function () {
        this.series.forEach(function (series) {
          series.points.forEach(function (point) {
            if (point.dataLabel &amp;&amp; point.shapeArgs) {
              const radius = point.shapeArgs.r;
              const angle = point.shapeArgs.end - point.shapeArgs.start;
              const labelRadius = radius * 0.7;
              const maxOuterWidth = 2 * (radius - labelRadius);
              const maxSideWidth = 2 * labelRadius * Math.sin(angle / 2);
              let safeWidth = Math.min(maxOuterWidth, maxSideWidth) - 10;
              safeWidth = Math.max(0, safeWidth);

              point.dataLabel.css({
                width: Math.floor(safeWidth) + &quot;px&quot;,
                textOverflow: &quot;ellipsis&quot;,
                whiteSpace: &quot;nowrap&quot;,
                overflow: &quot;hidden&quot;
              });
            }
          });
        });
      }
    }
  },
</code></pre>
<p>Please see full demo: <a href="https://jsfiddle.net/BlackLabel/wtsrnbLz/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://jsfiddle.net/BlackLabel/wtsrnbLz/</a></p>
